│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ boundary_ring_optimization                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ Optimal Heilbronn configurations for n=13 are believed to lie on the boundary of a convex │
│                          │ polygon. I replace the random interior points with points on a circle (scale-invariant    │
│                          │ since the metric normalizes by hull area), and perform a deterministic seeded local       │
│                          │ optimization of the 13 angular positions to maximize the minimum triangle area over all   │
│                          │ C(13,3)=286 triangles. Triangle areas on a unit circle have a cheap closed form:          │
│                          │ 0.5*|sin(Δ1)+sin(Δ2)+sin(Δ3)|. Starting from a regular 13-gon, we apply adaptive random   │
│                          │ perturbations (accepting improvements) with fixed seed, which converges quickly and       │
│                          │ reproducibly to a strong configuration.                                                   │
