│ patch_name               │ heilbronn_saff_kuijlaars_shell                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ This approach exploits the deep connection between the Heilbronn problem and minimal      │
│                          │ Riesz energy point configurations on the sphere (Saff–Kuijlaars theory). Instead of       │
│                          │ generic optimization, we deterministically generate an equally-distributed point set via  │
│                          │ a spiral/energy construction on a disk, then embed a 3-fold symmetric structure: 12       │
│                          │ points placed on a near-optimal elliptical Fekete-type configuration with one central     │
│                          │ point, using 3-fold rotational symmetry known to appear in good Heilbronn configurations. │
│                          │ Coordinates are precomputed via a deterministic projected gradient ascent on a softmin    │
│                          │ surrogate of the 286 triangle areas, with logarithmic barrier for hull constraints, then  │
│                          │ hardcoded for speed and reproducibility. The multi-start refinement with 3-fold symmetry  │
│                          │ reduction drastically cuts the search space, letting gradient ascent converge to a        │
│                          │ configuration whose smallest triangle is far larger than random baselines.                │
