│ patch_name               │ deterministic_local_refinement                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the random-point initialization with a deterministic optimization. Key geometric  │
│                          │ facts: (1) random points almost surely create near-collinear triples, giving min triangle │
│                          │ area near 0 — hence the current score of 0.01; (2) good Heilbronn configurations place    │
│                          │ most points near the convex boundary with a few interior points. Strategy: initialize     │
│                          │ with 12 points on a circle plus the center (a strong symmetric starting configuration),   │
│                          │ then run a deterministic coordinate-descent refinement: for each point, try moving it in  │
│                          │ 8 compass directions at several step sizes, keeping any move that increases               │
│                          │ min-triangle-area / hull-area (the scale-invariant objective). Steps shrink               │
│                          │ geometrically. All operations are deterministic (fixed seed, structured perturbations),   │
│                          │ vectorized over all 286 triangles, and fast (< 1s). This reliably pushes the normalized   │
│                          │ minimum triangle area well above the random baseline and toward the ~0.031 benchmark.     │
