│ patch_name               │ vectorized_ratio_gradient_heilbronn13                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ This crossover keeps the structure of the current program (deterministic multi-seed       │
│                          │ optimization returning a (13,2) array, rescaled so the convex hull has unit area) but     │
│                          │ replaces the slow Python triple loop and the box-barrier with a fully vectorized,         │
│                          │ scale-invariant formulation. Key improvements: (1) all 286 triangle areas and their       │
│                          │ gradients are computed with precomputed index arrays and `np.add.at` scatter (no Python   │
│                          │ loops); (2) the objective is the actual metric, min_area/hull_area, via a softmin         │
│                          │ gradient on triangle areas combined with a `-∇log(hull_area)` term, which is affine/scale │
│                          │ invariant so no boundary barriers are needed; (3) multiple deterministic initializations  │
│                          │ (regular 13-gon, 3-fold symmetric, random disk points) with more iterations become        │
│                          │ affordable; (4) a final exact hill-climb on single-point perturbations polishes the best  │
│                          │ configuration. This combines the correctness of the gradient approach from the current    │
│                          │ program with far more optimization within the same time budget, which should              │
│                          │ substantially raise min_area_normalized and the combined score.                           │
