│ patch_name               │ heilbronn13_sym_search                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ This crossover combines the best elements of both prior programs: it keeps the fully      │
│                          │ vectorized triangle-area machinery (_cross_all with precomputed index arrays), the        │
│                          │ efficient log-ratio gradient ascent (_optimize), and the coordinate-polish stage from the │
│                          │ current program, while adding a key new ingredient motivated by the heuristic knowledge   │
│                          │ that optimal Heilbronn configurations for n=13 exhibit 3-fold rotational symmetry. Since  │
│                          │ 13 = 1 + 3+3+3+3, the search space is dramatically reduced by parametrizing the           │
│                          │ configuration as a center point plus 4 rotational orbits (radius + phase each, 8          │
│                          │ parameters). A fast deterministic random search over this compact 8-D space finds strong  │
│                          │ symmetric candidates, which are then refined by gradient ascent on log(min-area) -        │
│                          │ log(hull-area) and a coordinate-level polish. This gives global exploration (random       │
│                          │ search over symmetric parametrization) combined with local exploitation (gradient +       │
│                          │ polish), and is faster than the previous multi-start since the symmetric parametrization  │
│                          │ collapses a 26-D search into 8-D. Determinism is preserved via fixed seeds, and the final │
│                          │ configuration is rescaled so the convex hull has unit area.                               │
