│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ vectorized_min_area_and_multistart_optimization                                           │
│ patch_description        │ Two targeted improvements. (1) Fully vectorize the smallest-triangle computation using a  │
│                          │ precomputed combination index matrix, so each score evaluation is a single vectorized     │
│                          │ cross-product computation over all 286 triples instead of a Python loop; this roughly     │
│                          │ cuts scoring cost several-fold and lets the optimizer do many more descent steps within   │
│                          │ the same time budget. (2) Replace the single seed (12-gon + center, which is limited by   │
│                          │ center-point triples) with a deterministic multi-start strategy over several structured,  │
│                          │ symmetry-informed seeds (regular 13-gon, 12-gon+center, perturbed circle, 3-fold          │
│                          │ symmetric ring configuration), refining each by coordinate descent and returning the      │
│                          │ best-scoring configuration. Multi-start mitigates the poor local optimum of a single seed │
│                          │ while keeping determinism (no RNG, or fixed-seed perturbations). Empirically,             │
│                          │ boundary-heavy configurations such as near-regular 13-gons give much larger minimum       │
│                          │ triangle areas for n=13 than configurations with interior points, so seeding with         │
│                          │ boundary-focused candidates directly targets the score.                                   │
