│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ ratio_objective_adaptive_steps                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ The current code optimizes the raw minimum triangle area while clipping points into a     │
│                          │ fixed unit-area hexagon. But the scoring metric is min_triangle_area / hull_area(points), │
│                          │ where the hull is the convex hull of the 13 points themselves — not the hexagon. Two      │
│                          │ consequences:                                                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. The optimizer's objective (raw min area inside the hexagon) is misaligned with the     │
│                          │ true metric. Shrinking the hull (pulling points inward) reduces the denominator and can   │
│                          │ increase the normalized score even at constant raw min area. The optimizer should         │
│                          │ directly maximize min_area/hull_area.                                                     │
│                          │ 2. A single global step size means one stuck point (e.g., a hull vertex that cannot move  │
│                          │ outward) throttles refinement for all points. The recommendation suggests per-point       │
│                          │ adaptive step sizes: halve only the failing point's step, and occasionally re-grow steps. │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The edit replaces the hard-min optimizer with a ratio-based one that:                     │
│                          │ - uses the monotone-chain hull area as denominator (computed on the fly, cheap for 13     │
│                          │ points),                                                                                  │
│                          │ - maintains a per-point step vector, halving only steps whose trials fail and multiplying │
│                          │ successful steps by 1.3 (capped),                                                         │
│                          │ - tries both an objective-ascent move and a random perturbation per point per sweep,      │
│                          │ - no longer forces points into the hexagon (only a mild centering/repulsion keeps the     │
│                          │ configuration non-degenerate); instead the hull of the points defines the region.         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This directly targets combined_score = min_area/hull_area / 0.0309.                       │
