│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ vectorized_softmin_gradient_and_polish                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ The current program loses to the earlier vectorized soft-min gradient approach (0.70 vs   │
│                          │ 0.75) because its hill climbing is slow and gets stuck. The fix: (1) add a fast, fully    │
│                          │ vectorized soft-min gradient ascent optimizer (exact analytic gradient of a               │
│                          │ LogSumExp-smoothed minimum of all 286 triangle areas, with annealed sharpness) applied to │
│                          │ every seed; (2) run the expensive exact hill-climb polish only on the top few candidates  │
│                          │ rather than every seed; (3) add a basin-hopping style deterministic                       │
│                          │ perturbation-and-restart around the best solution, which directly attacks the             │
│                          │ local-optimum limitation. This keeps determinism (fixed seeds, fixed perturbations) while │
│                          │ substantially improving the achieved minimum-triangle area and reducing runtime.          │
