│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ adaptive_per_point_polish                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ The gradient ascent only optimizes a soft-min surrogate; the final score is the true hard │
│                          │ min of triangle areas normalized by hull area. I add a deterministic hill-climb polishing │
│                          │ stage that directly maximizes the true score, with **adaptive per-point step sizes** (per │
│                          │ the recommendation): each point keeps its own step, halved when none of its trial moves   │
│                          │ improve, and occasionally regrown (×1.5, capped at 0.25) when a point has been skipped    │
│                          │ for many sweeps. This lets constrained points refine finely while hull points keep        │
│                          │ exploring, avoiding premature global step collapse. We polish only the top few            │
│                          │ gradient-optimized candidates to keep runtime bounded, then take the best true score      │
│                          │ across all candidates.                                                                    │
