│ patch_name               │ hardmin_multistart_coordinate_descent                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the soft-min gradient ascent + gentle hill-climb pipeline with a hard-min         │
│                          │ coordinate-descent optimizer applied directly to the true objective (min triangle area /  │
│                          │ hull area). Coordinate descent on the exact hard min has previously proven ~3.5x more     │
│                          │ effective than soft-min gradients because the LogSumExp smoothing wastes effort raising   │
│                          │ near-min triangles that never become the bottleneck. Additionally, add structurally       │
│                          │ diverse full-configuration seeds (two concentric rings 7+5+center, hexagonal lattice,     │
│                          │ golden-ratio-perturbed circle) so the optimizer can escape the 3-fold-symmetric basin —   │
│                          │ known Heilbronn-13 optima are irregular, so symmetry-constrained initialization likely    │
│                          │ limits the achievable score. Each seed is polished with hard-min descent and only kept if │
│                          │ its final true score beats the running best. All randomness is seeded, so results stay    │
│                          │ deterministic. Vectorized triangle/hull computation keeps each objective evaluation cheap │
│                          │ (~286 triangles), so the descent converges in well under a second per seed.               │
