│ patch_name               │ extended_directions_multistart                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ The current coordinate-descent can only move points along 4 orientation axes (8           │
│                          │ directions). Known good Heilbronn configurations for n=13 are irregular, so the descent   │
│                          │ gets stuck in ring-symmetric local optima. Two targeted changes: (1) extend the direction │
│                          │ set to 16 directions at 22.5° increments, allowing the search to break the initial        │
│                          │ 12-fold symmetry; (2) run the refinement from multiple deterministic initializations      │
│                          │ (circle+center, slightly perturbed circle with fixed seed, and a jittered grid), keeping  │
│                          │ the best result. This is cheap and improves the chance of finding a configuration beating │
│                          │ the normalized benchmark.                                                                 │
