│ patch_name               │ add_hill_climb_refinement_and_random_seeds                                                │
│ patch_description        │ The best prior program (combined_score 0.80) used exact-ratio stochastic coordinate hill  │
│                          │ climbing with basin hopping, while the current gradient-only version scores 0.18. The     │
│                          │ softmin gradient ascent tends to stall in shallow basins because the smooth approximation │
│                          │ of the min is a poor guide near the kinked true objective. The fix: (1) add a             │
│                          │ single-point-move stochastic hill climber on the exact ratio _ratio, with adaptive step   │
│                          │ size; (2) run it as a refinement stage after each gradient run and again as a long final  │
│                          │ polish on the global best (this combines the gradient's fast basin approach with the      │
│                          │ climber's exact objective); (3) add fully asymmetric random 13-point seeds passed through │
│                          │ the same pipeline, per the recommendation to break the symmetry trap of the 3-fold        │
│                          │ parametrization. Determinism is preserved via fixed seeds.                                │
