│ patch_name               │ wide_funnel_softmin_polish13                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ The current program spends its 17s budget on only 16 seeds each followed by expensive     │
│                          │ exact hill-climbing. The funnel design principle says: broad cheap global search first,   │
│                          │ expensive exact refinement last. New configuration: (1) ~72 diverse deterministic seeds   │
│                          │ (polygons, double/triple rings, 3-fold symmetric orbits, jittered lattices, seeded random │
│                          │ restarts); (2) a fast vectorized softmin-gradient ascent (~300 iterations, annealed       │
│                          │ sharpness) on every seed to pull each toward a good basin — this is cheap because it uses │
│                          │ vectorized bincount gradients rather than exact evaluations; (3) rank all candidates by   │
│                          │ the exact ratio (min triangle area / hull area); (4) exact stochastic hill-climbing       │
│                          │ polish (single-point moves with adaptive amplitude and restart-on-improvement) on the top │
│                          │ 12 candidates, with a time-budget guard. This broadens multi-start coverage ~4.5x while   │
│                          │ keeping per-candidate cost low, which is the demonstrated mechanism for escaping the 0.02 │
│                          │ plateau. Determinism is preserved via fixed seeds and no wall-clock dependence in results │
│                          │ (the time guard only caps work, and iteration counts are fixed).                          │
