│                          │ library (double-ring configurations across multiple radii, 3-fold symmetric orbits,       │
│                          │ jittered lattices, seeded random restarts), elite selection (top-14 candidates polished   │
│                          │ with per-rank deterministic seeds), a multi-elite basin-hopping stage with an amplitude   │
│                          │ ladder, hull-expansion probes, and a longer final polish. From the hexagon-based          │
│                          │ inspiration we add dual-ring hexagonal seeds (6+6 rings + center at varying radii), which │
│                          │ historically produce good Heilbronn basins. The result should recover the ~0.84           │
│                          │ combined-score behavior while remaining fully deterministic and reasonably fast.          │
