╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ streamline_grad_and_expand_basin_hopping                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ The main inefficiencies: (1) `grad_ascent` contains dead placeholder code (an empty       │
│                          │ analytic loop, a dead `np.add.at`) and runs a full numeric gradient through `score` with  │
│                          │ a C(13,3)=286-triangle evaluation per coordinate — very slow with negligible benefit. We  │
│                          │ replace it with a lean, corrected version that computes the finite-difference gradient    │
│                          │ only on a subset of promising directions using the true smooth score, with adaptive step. │
│                          │ (2) Basin hopping is expanded per the recommendation: 8 perturbations across amplitudes   │
│                          │ drawn from a deterministic schedule, applied to the top-3 elites (not just the best),     │
│                          │ each followed by grad_ascent + hill_climb. This is the proven-cheap extension suggested   │
│                          │ and reuses existing machinery. Time budget should remain similar because grad_ascent      │
