│ patch_description        │ Adapts the best-performing prior architecture (3-fold rotational symmetry via a 4-point   │
│                          │ base expanded to 12 points plus center, softmin gradient ascent screening, then exact     │
│                          │ hill-climb polish), but scales it up per the recommendation: ~70 random base seeds (up    │
│                          │ from 24), 8 structured seeds, and exact hill-climb polish on the top 10 candidates (up    │
│                          │ from 4), plus more basin-hopping kicks. The softmin gradient stage is cheap (300          │
│                          │ vectorized iterations over 286 triples), so widening the funnel fits comfortably in the   │
│                          │ runtime budget. The 3-fold symmetric parameterization (13 points determined by 4 base     │
│                          │ points, i.e., an 8-dimensional search) was exactly what broke the 0.02 plateau, so we     │
│                          │ keep it as the core and simply multiply multi-start breadth, which the recommendation     │
│                          │ identifies as the key lever.                                                              │
