│ patch_description        │ Builds on the current 3-fold symmetric multi-start (4 base points -> 12 rotated points +  │
│                          │ center). Key improvements per the recommendations:                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Hull-expansion move**: in the symmetric refine stage and polish stage, periodically  │
│                          │ try scaling all points outward by 1.01× (about the hull centroid). This reduces the       │
│                          │ hull-area denominator of the true score; it is accepted only when the true                │
│                          │ min_area/hull_area score strictly improves. Since expansion also increases min triangle   │
│                          │ area in absolute terms, this often gains score when points hug the hull boundary.         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Sharper guidance blend**: the internal hill-climb objective uses 0.8·min + 0.2·(mean │
│                          │ of 3 smallest areas), a sharper approximation of the true min than the previous           │
│                          │ 0.6/0.4-over-5 blend. Final selection across seeds always uses the exact min/hull ratio,  │
│                          │ so the reported metric is never diluted by the blend.                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. Vectorized triangle-area evaluation with incremental updates for single-point moves    │
│                          │ keeps evaluation fast; overall runtime stays within a few seconds.                        │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
