│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ optimize_true_ratio_objective                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ The refinement stages currently maximize the raw minimum triangle area while ignoring the │
│                          │ convex hull area in the denominator. Since the benchmark score is min_area/hull_area, a   │
│                          │ configuration can be improved both by increasing the min triangle AND by shrinking the    │
│                          │ hull (e.g., pulling near-boundary "wasted" points inward so that small triangles with     │
│                          │ them grow relative to hull area). I make three consistent changes:                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Refinement (`_refine_base` and `_polish_full`) now directly maximize the true          │
│                          │ objective `_true_score` (min area / hull area) rather than raw min area. The pattern      │
│                          │ search remains deterministic; each candidate is scored with the full ratio, so the        │
│                          │ optimizer can trade hull shrinkage against triangle growth — this is the key geometric    │
│                          │ insight: many near-optimal Heilbronn configurations sit strictly inside their hull, and   │
│                          │ fixing the hull (as the hexagon-clipped earlier programs did) is suboptimal.              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. Vectorize `_hull_area` with `scipy.spatial.ConvexHull` (with a pure-numpy fallback) as │
│                          │ recommended: pattern search calls the score hundreds of times per sweep, so this          │
│                          │ multiplies the number of seeds/steps affordable in the same runtime.                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. Increase the deterministic seed pool (more 3-fold symmetric radial seeds plus more     │
│                          │ random seeds) to exploit the cheaper scoring, and use a slightly finer polish step. All   │
│                          │ seeds remain fixed/seeded, preserving determinism.                                        │
