│ patch_name               │ multi_elite_basin_hopping                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ The recommendation suggests extending the current basin-hopping idea into a               │
│                          │ multi-amplitude restart scheme applied to the top-3 ranked candidates rather than only    │
│                          │ the single best. Currently the main loop refines each seed independently and simply keeps │
│                          │ the global best, throwing away all other strong local optima. Multiple distinct local     │
│                          │ optima often sit near each other; deterministic sinusoidal perturbations at several       │
│                          │ amplitudes (0.01–0.08) around each elite, followed by short coordinate-descent re-polish  │
│                          │ (_polish_full) and (optionally) base-space re-refinement, can hop into better basins. The │
│                          │ scheme is fully deterministic (fixed amplitude list, fixed per-point deterministic        │
│                          │ pseudo-random signs), so reproducibility is preserved. Eval budget: 3 elites × 6          │
│                          │ amplitudes × short polish — modest overhead given the current 8.7s runtime. Selection of  │
│                          │ elites is by true score; the kick uses a fixed deterministic direction field (sinusoidal  │
│                          │ pattern) applied to all 13 points, with a symmetric negative variant to double coverage   │
│                          │ cheaply.                                                                                  │
