│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ two_pass_exact_funnel_13pt                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ The key weakness is ranking ~80 softmin gradient-ascent candidates purely by the          │
│                          │ softmin-derived exact score, then polishing only top-4 — softmin-optimal candidates can   │
│                          │ be exact-poor near plateaus. This rewrite implements a two-pass funnel: (1) generate ~60  │
│                          │ diverse seeds (3-fold symmetric expansions, two-ring hexagons, 7+5 ring, jittered         │
│                          │ circles, seeded random), (2) cheap 3-step mini exact hill-climb on ALL candidates to      │
│                          │ re-rank with the true objective, (3) full exact coordinate-descent polish (multi-step,    │
│                          │ shrinking steps, 8 directions) on the re-ranked top-10, (4) deterministic basin-hopping   │
│                          │ around the best with re-descend. Key parameters changed: mini-climb re-ranking            │
│                          │ (steps_max=3, step=0.02) for all candidates; polish slots raised 4→10; polish uses 8      │
│                          │ directions with step halving to 1e-5; exact-objective polish only (no blended surrogate   │
│                          │ ranking). Runtime kept under ~20s by bounding mini-climb work.                            │
