│ patch_description        │ The blended surrogate `score()` (0.6·min + 0.4·mean-of-smallest-5) optimizes a different  │
│                          │ quantity than the graded metric, which is the pure minimum triangle area. Near a plateau, │
│                          │ surrogate-optimal points can be exact-poor. Two targeted changes: (1) after the surrogate │
│                          │ `fine_polish`, run a final coordinate hill-climb directly on `true_score` so the last     │
│                          │ refinement pushes the actual graded objective; (2) since the true polish may move points, │
│                          │ re-verify with `true_score` and accept on any non-negative improvement (ties accepted to  │
│                          │ allow lateral exploration of flat directions that may later yield gains via diagonal      │
│                          │ moves). This is cheap (286 triangles vectorized) and deterministic, directly targeting    │
│                          │ min_area_normalized rather than the proxy.                                                │
