│ patch_name               │ hullshrink_score_opt                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The plateau at min_area_normalized ≈ 0.03 comes from two issues: (1) the softmin-free     │
│                          │ pattern search accepts moves on min-area alone, ignoring that score = min_area /          │
│                          │ hull_area, and (2) the hull denominator is never actively minimized. Key changes: (a)     │
│                          │ every accepted move in both the base refinement and the full polish is now gated on the   │
│                          │ exact true score (min_area / hull_area), with scipy's ConvexHull for fast hull-area       │
│                          │ evaluation; (b) a new hull-reduction move set — hull vertices get extra inward radial and │
│                          │ centroid-pulling candidate directions (multiplicative contraction per hull point),        │
│                          │ letting the optimizer shrink the hull while holding min area, which directly raises the   │
│                          │ ratio; (c) periodic global contraction attempts (scale points toward centroid, repeat     │
│                          │ while the true score improves); (d) reduced seed count and a tighter polish min_step      │
│                          │ (5e-4) plus a bounded basin-hopping stage (2 elites × 3 amplitudes) to keep eval_time     │
│                          │ well under the previous 30s. All moves deterministic; seed 42 retained.                   │
